%% Logical sequence. "Store" includes reconstruction, the journal, project files and Git.
%% The commit pipeline is drawn in detail in commit_pipeline.mmd.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Developer
    participant UI as Front end / cascade loop
    participant App as Application API
    participant S as Session
    participant P as Planner / review
    participant Q as Scheduler / locks
    participant A as Runner / adapters
    participant C as Commit pipeline
    participant N as Store / files / Git

    User->>UI: Submit task (or --recover)
    UI->>App: RunRequest (same shape from mak run and the app)
    App->>App: Discover config, apply overrides, resolve planner route and key
    App->>S: Build session (registry, health preflight)
    S->>S: Take exclusive project lease
    S->>N: Recover interrupted commit journal

    alt New task
        S->>Q: Clear lock table (lease proves prior owner is gone)
        S->>N: Load .makignore, reconcile store with working tree
        S->>P: Plan over the planning index (inventory view, dependency graph)
        loop retrieval strategy, at most max_expansions rounds
            P->>P: Model asks to expand files or directories, within the token budget
        end
        P-->>S: SubTask plan with declarations (changes_api, contract, registry_keys)
        S->>S: Validate plan against the dependency graph, add caller-update tasks
        opt Plan review enabled
            S->>User: Show plan, findings and MAK-proposed tasks
            User-->>S: Approve, edit, drop MAK tasks, or abort
        end
        S->>Q: install_plan: re-validate, assign agents, start WaveState, persist task graph
    else Resume interrupted run
        S->>Q: Expire stale leases, rebuild scheduler and WaveState from task_graph.json
    end

    par Heartbeat thread
        S->>Q: Renew leases, scan for deadlocks
    and Run loop, while work remains and the spend ceiling holds
        loop Each tick
            S->>Q: Tick ready queue
            Q->>Q: lock_requests per task, try_acquire_all (all or nothing)
            Note over Q,A: Contended tasks wait holding nothing. Independent tasks run concurrently.
            Q->>S: Ready tasks with their grants
            S->>N: Enrich bundle: contracts, targets, context, siblings, callers, dependency outputs
            S->>S: Capture read set, refuse a starved bundle
            S->>A: Dispatch on the bounded thread pool
            A->>A: Structured call, check stop signal, one repair turn if malformed
            A-->>S: TaskResult (new_sources, usage, stop_reason)
            S->>S: Map returned ids onto the grant, compile() each fragment, stage
            Note over S,C: Concurrent completions form one batch, committed in topological order
            S->>C: Run the ordered checks
            alt accept
                C->>N: Transaction: commit versions, journal, install files atomically
                N->>N: Metadata save is the commit point, then [MAK-id] audit commit
                C->>Q: Release grants, complete the task or narrow the remainder
            else defer
                C->>S: Park the result until a lock or contract provider frees
            else reject, resend or fail
                C->>N: Roll back staged fragments
                C->>Q: Release locks, re-dispatch with a retry note or mark failed
            end
            S->>C: Resume parked commits after each batch
        end
    end
    S-->>UI: Wave result (completed, failed, skipped, blocked)

    loop Cascade, until clean, declined, stalled, oscillating or max_waves
        UI->>S: Detect fix-ups: reference-graph cascade, cross-module defects, gates
        S-->>UI: Fix-up tasks with repair obligations, or none
        opt Fix-up tasks found
            UI->>User: Review fix-up wave
            User-->>UI: Approve, edit or decline
            opt Approved
                UI->>S: install_plan and run the same loop
                Note over S,C: A repair commits only if its obligations hold prospectively
                S-->>UI: Fix-up wave result
            end
        end
    end

    UI->>S: Teardown with the aggregate ExecutionResult
    S->>S: Run tests: passed / failed / skipped / error
    opt auto_push, request satisfied, and test policy met
        S->>N: Push Git audit history
    end
    S-->>UI: Test outcome, push result or the gate that refused
    UI->>S: Close workers, release project lease
    UI-->>User: Report completed, failed, blocked and unresolved work
